{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Cross-implementation edge cases (spec §11). recovery_key_display_valid: decodeRecoveryKey(input) MUST return rk; recovery_key_display_invalid: decoding is ASCII-only and MUST fail. x25519_*: wrong-length keys MUST fail with bad_request (public key derivation, X25519, unwrapFromDevice, wrapToDevice with recipient.kx_pub b64 and ephemeral_secret). ed25519_valid: verifyObject(context, object, public_key) MUST succeed; ed25519_invalid: MUST fail with invalid_signature under strict RFC 8032 (S < L, canonical A and R, no small-order A, cofactorless equation); all but s_not_reduced verify under a lenient ZIP-215 cofactored verifier.",
